## Summary

Worked the sole failing ship-gate criterion (`cache_coherency` / `test_unlink_visibility`); 11/12 still pass. Two code changes landed (build `1371EA35`), and the root cause was narrowed decisively through RULE-4 instrumentation + one RULE-5 Gemini consult.

**Changes made (both KEEP):**
1. **Modify-time tenure stamping** — moved `b_tenure_id` stamping from read-time (3 sites: xfs_btree/xfs_ialloc/xfs_alloc) to modify-time in `mxfs_ag_meta_track`. A cache-hit read no longer re-stamps a prior-tenure stale buffer "current". Verified: no regression, timing fast, preserves the sess123 AGI fix. (P124 still fires — residual is the in_ail ghost, which no tenure stamp can reach.)
2. **Dir-flush reorder** — moved `mxfs_dir_flush_data_blocks` after the sess29 settle so committed dir blocks are visible as IN_AIL and flushed out of the AIL before DLM handoff (Gemini Q1). Architecturally correct for EXTENTS dirs; no regression.

**Root cause (corrected, sharp):** Not the shortform parent — I *disproved* that (the merged 4-node `P-SFDIR-RELOAD ino=131` timeline shows node1 reloads the parent with `count=2 [test_unlink unlink_vis]` and keeps it). The real bug is **reused-inode stale-cache on the winner directory inode** (4194433): node1's in-core copy is a stale *freed* incarnation (`incore_mode=00, incore_gen=disk_gen+1`) while disk has the live dir (`040755, nlink=2`). node1 resolves the name correctly but serves its mode=0 cached inode → readdir sees 0, create/rm hit ENOENT. `d_revalidate` fails to evict it because its GENMISS/TYPEMISS FUA rechecks are gated on `S_ISDIR(incore mode)`, which is false when the cached mode is 0. node4 passes because its cached copy is live.

**Next session (concrete, in `state.md` + memory `sess125-shortform-parent-dir-lost-update-is-the-root`):**
1. Cheap fix first: in `mxfs_drevalidate`, when a positive dentry resolves to the same ino but the in-core `i_mode == 0`, run the lockless FUA `di_gen/di_mode` recheck unconditionally (drop the `S_ISDIR(incore)` gate for the mode-0 case) → mark stale + evict → re-iget the live dir. Measure node1 `actual=120`; watch for sess91 ISTALE-CAW thrash / rename regression.
2. Deeper/true root: make `xfs_iget_cache_hit` reload a dir inode cached as mode-0 when a peer/dirent shows it live, instead of returning the stale freed incarnation.

Gemini consult #1 done this session; if the above two attempts fail, do Gemini consult #2 then escalate to GPT per the RULE-5 chain.

